## 2. Key Architecture Decisions

| Decision | Choice | Rationale |
|---|---|---|
| **Task queue** | **ARQ** (not Celery) | Async-native (matches FastAPI), lighter footprint, Redis-backed (already in stack), simpler config. Celery's multi-broker support is unnecessary here. |
| **Hexagonal architecture** | Domain layer has zero framework imports | Testable in isolation, portable, enforced by linting rules |
| **Auth** | OAuth2 password flow + JWT (access 15m / refresh 7d) + Argon2id | Standard, stateless verification, refresh rotation with revocation list in Redis |
| **Multi-tenancy** | Shared DB, `tenant_id` on every row, PostgreSQL RLS policies | Cost-efficient, strong isolation, tested with dedicated suite |
| **Telemetry storage** | TimescaleDB hypertable partitioned by `device_id` + time | Purpose-built for time-series, continuous aggregates for rollups, compression + retention policies |
| **ML model registry** | File-based with DB metadata (ModelVersion table) | Simple, no external dependency; S3-compatible interface for production upgrade |
| **Config** | pydantic-settings, 12-factor, `.env` files per environment | Type-safe, validated at startup |
| **Package manager** | **uv** | Fastest resolver, lockfile support, drop-in pip replacement |

